---
import BlogPostLayout from "../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro";
import BlogByline from "../../components/BlogByline.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";

// Make this page dynamic via SSR
export const prerender = false;

const publishDate = new Date("November 9 2026");
const readTime = "5 min read";

const isPublished = new Date().getTime() >= publishDate.getTime();

---

<BlogPostLayout
  title="What Service Taught Us: Veterans Day"
  schemaTitle="What Service Taught Us About Running a Company (A Veterans Day Note)"
  description={isPublished ? "A Veterans Day note from a veteran- and woman-owned cleaning company: the two habits the Air Force taught our founder, and how they show up in your house every visit." : "Coming Soon: What Service Taught Us About Running a Company (A Veterans Day Note)"}
  noindex={!isPublished}
  publishDate={publishDate}
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center">
        <span class="inline-block px-4 py-2 bg-[#FFA985]/20 text-[#FFA985] rounded-full text-sm font-medium mb-6">
          Brand Story/Trust
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">
          What Service Taught Us About Running a Company
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          {isPublished ? "A Veterans Day note from a veteran- and woman-owned company." : "Coming November 9 2026."}
        </p>
        <div class="mb-8">
          <BlogByline variant="dark" date={publishDate} readTime={readTime} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Content Toggle based on Published Date -->
  {isPublished ? (
    <article class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <h2>First, the important part</h2>
<p><strong>Happy Veterans Day to everyone who served — and to the families who served alongside them. If that's you: thank you. The rest of this post is about what those years taught us, but that first line is the point of the day.</strong></p>

<h3>The two habits that followed Todd home</h3>
<p>Todd, our founder, is an Air Force veteran. He'll be the first to tell you that "military precision" has become a cleaning-industry cliché — every company with a veteran on the truck puts it on a flyer. So instead of the slogan, here are the two habits that actually followed him out of the service and into this company.</p>

<h4>1. Write it down</h4>
<p>The Air Force doesn't trust memory, and not because its people aren't sharp — because everyone forgets things when the work is routine. Aircraft fly on written checklists for exactly that reason. So do our cleans: the same 44-item checklist on every regular visit, 57 items on a deep clean, worked in the same order every time. The result never depends on what someone happened to notice that day.</p>

<h4>2. Own the result</h4>
<p>The other habit is harder to put on a flyer: when something goes wrong, you say so, and you fix it. In this company that means if we missed something, you tell us within 24 hours and we'll get a re-clean on the schedule right away, at no charge. No forms, no argument. You shouldn't have to chase your cleaning company for an answer.</p>

<h3>The military community around here</h3>
<p>We serve a lot of military families — Redstone Arsenal is in our backyard, and Todd has been the guy in-processing with a house full of boxes. PCS moves, TDYs, deployments: we know what a move-out clean means when the housing inspection is Thursday. Veterans and active-duty service members get 15% off every service, in every market we serve. Mention it when you call and we apply it before you book.</p>

<h3>If you'd like us to handle the house</h3>
<p><strong>Call (256) 826-1100, tell us your square footage and the type of cleaning, and you'll have your exact price before you hang up — the number we quote is the number we bill.</strong> Background-checked cleaners and $2 million in liability insurance on every visit.</p>
<p>And whether you call us or not: to everyone who wore the uniform, thank you for your service.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  ) : (
    <article class="py-16 bg-white border-t border-gray-100 shadow-inner">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-center">
          <Icon name="clock" class="w-16 h-16 text-[#FFA985] mx-auto mb-6" />
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 mt-0">Article Coming Soon!</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">This article is locked and scheduled to automatically publish on <br/><strong class="text-gray-800 text-xl">November 9 2026</strong>.<br/>Check back then!</p>
          <div class="mt-12">
            <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 text-lg font-semibold text-white bg-[#FFA985] rounded-full hover:bg-[#ff9a70] transition shadow-md no-underline">
              Back to Blog
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  )}
</BlogPostLayout>
